--- code
export async function claimsSchemeThroughStandardApi(
  scheme: PostingScheme,
  formatName: string,
): Promise<boolean> {
  return requestSchemeAccess(schemeIdOf(scheme), [{ formatName }]).then(
    () => true,
    () => false,
  );
}
--- callers
// postings/warmup/PostingWarmUp.ts
export async function warmUpPosting(scheme: PostingScheme, formatName: string): Promise<void> {
  if (!(await claimsSchemeThroughStandardApi(scheme, formatName))) {
    return;
  }

  await openPostingSession(scheme, formatName);
}
--- facts
The standard scheme API rejects where a ledger refuses the scheme, and it resolves where the ledger takes it.

# claimed at this site by an earlier run:
The ledgers that ignore the settlement scheme are the ones whose first posting stalls.
combinationClaim, the claim for a combination, reports those ledgers as Unknown, so the posting warm-up gates on this function.
